1
00:00:05,005 --> 00:00:06,006
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION.

2
00:00:06,089 --> 00:00:07,925
THERE IS NO RELATION
TO REAL PEOPLE OR EVENTS.

3
00:00:11,595 --> 00:00:14,097
[♪ gentle music playing]

4
00:00:14,181 --> 00:00:15,182
- [camera shutter clicks]
- [typing]

5
00:00:16,099 --> 00:00:17,142
[grunts]

6
00:00:18,852 --> 00:00:20,896
We've got all the time in the world.

7
00:00:20,979 --> 00:00:22,856
No rush. [chuckles]

8
00:00:23,857 --> 00:00:26,026
Bask in the warm sunlight.

9
00:00:26,109 --> 00:00:27,110
[shutter clicking]

10
00:00:27,194 --> 00:00:29,738
Feel the gentle breeze against your skin.

11
00:00:30,239 --> 00:00:33,200
- Thank you for the tea.
- [grunts, chuckles]

12
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:34,701
[sighs]

13
00:00:34,785 --> 00:00:36,203
[typing continues]

14
00:00:38,622 --> 00:00:40,541
Both people and plants…

15
00:00:41,124 --> 00:00:44,419
We can't see the world around us
if we don't look up.

16
00:00:45,170 --> 00:00:47,881
Go about your whole life
with your head down,

17
00:00:47,965 --> 00:00:49,925
you'll only ever see your own two feet.

18
00:00:50,008 --> 00:00:51,593
[both chuckle]

19
00:00:51,677 --> 00:00:52,928
You've got a point there.

20
00:00:53,428 --> 00:00:56,390
Although I understand that logically,
I can't quite put it into practice.

21
00:00:56,473 --> 00:00:57,474
[Karin's grandfather] Mmm.

22
00:01:00,477 --> 00:01:01,520
All right, then.

23
00:01:02,020 --> 00:01:03,397
[both chuckle]

24
00:01:06,733 --> 00:01:09,820
[Karin's grandfather] So it seems to me
the end is finally in sight, eh?

25
00:01:09,903 --> 00:01:10,904
[Gyeongsu chuckles]

26
00:01:10,988 --> 00:01:15,784
Mr. Gyeongsu, I'm itchin' to meet
that boy of yours sometime soon.

27
00:01:16,785 --> 00:01:17,786
[both chuckle]

28
00:01:20,664 --> 00:01:23,792
Don't you think that Karin would like it
if Yubin came to visit?

29
00:01:24,543 --> 00:01:27,254
My son's a very kind
and handsome kid, y'know.

30
00:01:27,838 --> 00:01:29,339
Yubin's got a lot of great qualities.

31
00:01:29,423 --> 00:01:31,091
Oh, you don't say?

32
00:01:31,174 --> 00:01:32,217
[both chuckle]

33
00:01:32,301 --> 00:01:36,722
But I'm not giving up my seat
next to my sweet Karin that easily,

34
00:01:36,805 --> 00:01:38,807
even if Yubin is a handsome kid.
[chuckles]

35
00:01:38,890 --> 00:01:41,435
[chuckles] Oh, so that's how it is?

36
00:01:42,519 --> 00:01:43,645
[Karin] Wait a second.

37
00:01:44,271 --> 00:01:46,982
Why are you deciding
who I'm going to marry without me?

38
00:01:48,650 --> 00:01:51,570
[chuckling] Please accept my apologies.

39
00:01:53,613 --> 00:01:56,325
You said that he's really good-looking?

40
00:01:57,034 --> 00:01:58,035
Really good-looking.

41
00:01:58,744 --> 00:01:59,995
When will he be here?

42
00:02:00,078 --> 00:02:01,705
[chuckles]

43
00:02:01,788 --> 00:02:03,582
Hopefully he can come visit soon.

44
00:02:06,084 --> 00:02:07,502
[Yubin] Hey, boss!

45
00:02:09,421 --> 00:02:12,424
[♪ tender music playing]

46
00:02:19,473 --> 00:02:20,474
[chuckles]

47
00:02:24,019 --> 00:02:25,062
[Yubin grunts]

48
00:02:28,940 --> 00:02:30,025
Karin.

49
00:02:32,152 --> 00:02:33,153
I'm home.

50
00:02:34,363 --> 00:02:35,364
Welcome back.

51
00:02:36,698 --> 00:02:38,825
[chuckles]
Did something happen at your work?

52
00:02:38,909 --> 00:02:40,243
[sighs]

53
00:02:40,327 --> 00:02:41,328
I already…

54
00:02:42,412 --> 00:02:43,705
settled what I needed there.

55
00:02:44,623 --> 00:02:46,625
And now, I'm back to square one.

56
00:02:52,214 --> 00:02:53,465
Mmm?

57
00:02:53,548 --> 00:02:55,175
- [Yubin sighs]
- Mmm.

58
00:03:00,055 --> 00:03:01,264
[chuckles]

59
00:03:08,647 --> 00:03:11,525
EPISODE 8

60
00:03:12,401 --> 00:03:13,694
[in Korean] It's been forever.

61
00:03:16,113 --> 00:03:17,114
[sighs]

62
00:03:21,952 --> 00:03:24,454
TEN RULES

63
00:03:26,748 --> 00:03:27,791
[in English] Karin.

64
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:31,253
These rules… Let's make new ones.
What do you say?

65
00:03:31,336 --> 00:03:33,004
[chuckles] All right, sure.

66
00:03:33,088 --> 00:03:35,382
- Mmm.
- Okay.

67
00:03:37,634 --> 00:03:39,636
- Hmm?
- [in Korean] Yeah. Exactly.

68
00:03:41,596 --> 00:03:42,722
"Of… the… day…"

69
00:03:43,223 --> 00:03:44,724
- "The. End." Yeah, yeah.
- [in English] Is this okay?

70
00:03:44,808 --> 00:03:46,017
Okay.

71
00:03:46,101 --> 00:03:47,602
- [in Korean] "Of."
- Okay. "Of."

72
00:03:47,686 --> 00:03:49,354
- Mmm?
- "Each."

73
00:03:49,438 --> 00:03:50,814
[in English] Wow, nicely done.

74
00:03:51,398 --> 00:03:52,691
[in Korean] "Day." Wow.

75
00:03:52,774 --> 00:03:54,609
- [chuckles]
- You're doing great. "We."

76
00:03:55,735 --> 00:03:56,778
[both] "Happy."

77
00:03:57,696 --> 00:03:59,573
- [Yubin, in English] "At the end…"
- "End"?

78
00:03:59,656 --> 00:04:00,949
- "The day…"
- Oh?

79
00:04:01,032 --> 00:04:02,576
- "At the end of…"
- "Of…"

80
00:04:03,076 --> 00:04:04,077
"Of the…"

81
00:04:04,161 --> 00:04:05,287
- "Us…"
- "Us…"

82
00:04:05,370 --> 00:04:06,371
AT THE END OF THE DAY,

83
00:04:06,455 --> 00:04:07,873
WE MUST TELL EACH OTHER
ONE THING THAT MADE US HAPPY.

84
00:04:07,956 --> 00:04:08,999
[Karin, in English] "Happy." Good.

85
00:04:09,082 --> 00:04:10,542
- I think that's perfect.
- Nice.

86
00:04:11,251 --> 00:04:12,252
YUBIN AND KARIN'S NEW RULES

87
00:04:12,335 --> 00:04:14,212
1. WE ARE TO ALWAYS HAVE
BREAKFAST AND DINNER TOGETHER!

88
00:04:14,296 --> 00:04:15,755
2. AFTER EATING,
YUBIN WILL DO THE DISHES,

89
00:04:15,839 --> 00:04:17,591
AND KARIN WILL CLEAR THE TABLE…

90
00:04:17,674 --> 00:04:19,926
- Great!
- There. The new rules.

91
00:04:20,010 --> 00:04:22,679
- Mm-hmm. Our brand new rules. Mmm.
- Mmm.

92
00:04:24,014 --> 00:04:25,015
Mmm.

93
00:04:27,893 --> 00:04:29,895
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

94
00:04:32,689 --> 00:04:35,275
- [yelps]
- [laughs]

95
00:04:36,777 --> 00:04:37,861
[exclaims]

96
00:04:41,072 --> 00:04:43,742
- [laughing]
- [laughing]

97
00:04:46,453 --> 00:04:47,662
[Yubin exclaims]

98
00:04:47,746 --> 00:04:49,539
- [Karin yelps]
- [laughs]

99
00:04:49,623 --> 00:04:51,625
- [Karin giggles]
- [Yubin exclaims]

100
00:04:51,708 --> 00:04:53,418
[groans] Hold on!

101
00:04:54,127 --> 00:04:55,504
[Karin exclaims]

102
00:04:56,588 --> 00:04:57,672
[both laughing]

103
00:05:00,133 --> 00:05:01,551
[Yubin, in Korean] Wow, this looks great.

104
00:05:03,428 --> 00:05:04,554
[both, in English] Time to eat.

105
00:05:07,098 --> 00:05:09,059
[in Korean] Mmm. Mmm, this is delicious.

106
00:05:09,142 --> 00:05:10,519
- Really?
- Mm-hmm.

107
00:05:11,186 --> 00:05:12,187
[Karin] Mmm.

108
00:05:12,270 --> 00:05:13,396
[in English] What do you call this dish?

109
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:15,816
<i>- Yasai no Nikumaki</i>.
- Mmm.

110
00:05:15,899 --> 00:05:18,735
Mmm. Mmm, Nikumaki, love it. Mmm.

111
00:05:18,819 --> 00:05:20,946
- You love it? [chuckles]
- Yeah. I love your cooking.

112
00:05:21,029 --> 00:05:22,781
- Thanks, Yubin.
- [humming]

113
00:05:23,365 --> 00:05:26,493
[singsongy, speaks Korean]
Squeaky, squeaky clean!

114
00:05:26,576 --> 00:05:27,911
[Yubin] Hmm?

115
00:05:27,994 --> 00:05:29,621
- [Karin, in English] Hey.
- Huh?

116
00:05:29,704 --> 00:05:31,331
- Yubin.
- Don't you like bubbles?

117
00:05:31,414 --> 00:05:33,291
It's not about that.
There are way too many!

118
00:05:33,375 --> 00:05:34,459
It's fine, it's fine.

119
00:05:34,543 --> 00:05:38,547
- [in Korean] The bubbles make them shiny.
- [in English] Switch with me.

120
00:05:38,630 --> 00:05:41,258
- [in Korean] I got it. Leave it to me.
- [in English] Hey, switch with me. You go.

121
00:05:41,341 --> 00:05:42,801
- [exclaims, laughs]
- [yelps]

122
00:05:42,884 --> 00:05:44,010
Hey!

123
00:05:44,094 --> 00:05:45,512
[in Korean] I got it.

124
00:05:53,645 --> 00:05:54,938
[in English] Mmm. Mm-hmm.

125
00:05:55,021 --> 00:05:57,566
- "Be careful not to…"
- Mm-hmm.

126
00:05:58,149 --> 00:06:01,278
- "…with an enemy around…"
- Mmm.

127
00:06:01,361 --> 00:06:02,737
- "Love's…"
- Yeah.

128
00:06:16,459 --> 00:06:19,087
- [in Korean] Karin! Karin. Hold on.
- Huh?

129
00:06:19,170 --> 00:06:20,547
[in English] Wait. Stay right there, okay?

130
00:06:20,630 --> 00:06:22,007
- Sure.
- Whoa.

131
00:06:22,966 --> 00:06:24,092
- What?
- You see this?

132
00:06:24,175 --> 00:06:26,177
[chuckles] What are you doing?

133
00:06:26,261 --> 00:06:27,929
- [in Korean] Look.
- [in English] I'm looking.

134
00:06:28,430 --> 00:06:29,431
Huh?

135
00:06:31,141 --> 00:06:34,227
[chuckles] Yubin!
What the heck are you doing?

136
00:06:34,311 --> 00:06:35,312
I'm blowing this up.

137
00:06:35,937 --> 00:06:37,355
- [chuckles]
- Your turn. Help me with this.

138
00:06:37,439 --> 00:06:40,984
- [Karin chuckling] Ooh, ooh.
- [chuckling]

139
00:06:47,532 --> 00:06:50,118
- [exclaims]
- [in Korean] Hold on. Hold on.

140
00:06:50,201 --> 00:06:51,911
[in English] Slow down. You're so fast!

141
00:07:25,528 --> 00:07:27,530
YUBIN'S ROOM

142
00:07:29,407 --> 00:07:31,159
This is your room starting today.

143
00:07:31,242 --> 00:07:32,744
Hey, what's… what's this?
Don't tell me you…

144
00:07:32,827 --> 00:07:34,454
- Is this for real?
- [in Korean] Yep. For real.

145
00:07:34,537 --> 00:07:36,456
[in English] Wait, but… but this is a bed!

146
00:07:36,539 --> 00:07:38,583
A bed-- Hey, it's an actual bed!

147
00:07:38,667 --> 00:07:40,960
Hey, it's…
It's actually a soft, fluffy bed!

148
00:07:41,044 --> 00:07:43,046
I mean, this is-- Hold on…

149
00:07:43,129 --> 00:07:45,340
- Hey, wait. Listen, listen, listen.
- I just meant this part--

150
00:07:45,423 --> 00:07:46,716
I built this bed all by myself.

151
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:49,010
You actually built this bed for me?

152
00:07:49,094 --> 00:07:50,637
- I'm so touched, it's really nice.
- You really like it?

153
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:51,721
- You like it?
- Yes. It's great.

154
00:07:51,805 --> 00:07:53,264
Okay, watch this. So every morning,

155
00:07:53,348 --> 00:07:54,641
- I'll… Every morning, I'll go…
- Yeah. Okay.

156
00:07:54,724 --> 00:07:56,267
- "Oh, hello. Good morning!"
- Mm-hmm. [chuckles]

157
00:07:56,351 --> 00:07:58,395
- Like this. And then, at night, I'll go…
- Like this. Uh-huh.

158
00:07:58,478 --> 00:08:00,563
- …"Sleep tight." Yeah?
- [chuckles]

159
00:08:00,647 --> 00:08:01,815
[both laughing]

160
00:08:03,274 --> 00:08:04,526
[Yubin] Is this heaven?

161
00:08:06,444 --> 00:08:07,445
[sighs]

162
00:08:08,446 --> 00:08:10,865
[in Korean] Guess nothing
is ever that easy.

163
00:08:19,290 --> 00:08:20,959
CHARO ISLAND'S ONLY ASAHI STORE

164
00:08:22,335 --> 00:08:23,545
- Oh!
- [gasps]

165
00:08:23,628 --> 00:08:24,629
[breathing shakily]

166
00:08:39,477 --> 00:08:40,603
RESUME
NAME PARK KUNAM

167
00:08:40,687 --> 00:08:42,188
[Asahi, in English]
<i>That's why he's been busy</i>

168
00:08:42,272 --> 00:08:43,732
<i>pounding the pavement,</i>
<i>looking for employment.</i>

169
00:08:46,484 --> 00:08:48,486
[♪ pensive music playing]

170
00:08:52,949 --> 00:08:54,576
Are you shopping for a matchmaking date?

171
00:08:54,659 --> 00:08:56,077
Oh, well, um…

172
00:08:56,161 --> 00:08:57,996
- Something like that, yes.
- [clerks] Aw!

173
00:08:58,079 --> 00:09:00,331
I wonder what type of girl she is.

174
00:09:00,415 --> 00:09:01,708
- I bet she's pretty.
- Right?

175
00:09:01,791 --> 00:09:05,795
Actually, uh, so… I have an important
job interview coming up this week,

176
00:09:05,879 --> 00:09:07,589
- and it's my first ever.
- [gasps]

177
00:09:07,672 --> 00:09:08,840
I don't have anything to wear.

178
00:09:09,466 --> 00:09:12,010
What made you decide to look for a job
all of a sudden?

179
00:09:12,093 --> 00:09:13,928
- [sucks teeth] Well…
- Mmm.

180
00:09:14,721 --> 00:09:18,808
Truthfully, I met someone I want
to spend the rest of my life with here.

181
00:09:18,892 --> 00:09:21,394
What? That's amazing!
You can ask me anything.

182
00:09:26,733 --> 00:09:27,734
[sighs]

183
00:09:36,201 --> 00:09:37,202
Mari, hi…

184
00:09:38,745 --> 00:09:39,871
Come inside.

185
00:09:50,882 --> 00:09:53,927
I'm guessing you skipped dinner,
didn't you?

186
00:09:54,010 --> 00:09:56,346
Hurry and eat first, before it gets cold.

187
00:10:00,558 --> 00:10:02,060
We can talk after you're done.

188
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:08,650
Thank you for the food.

189
00:10:15,949 --> 00:10:16,950
[sighs]

190
00:10:22,372 --> 00:10:23,706
Mari, I can…

191
00:10:25,416 --> 00:10:26,751
The truth is…

192
00:10:27,919 --> 00:10:29,170
I've been busy with…

193
00:10:34,259 --> 00:10:35,260
Kunam.

194
00:10:37,929 --> 00:10:39,347
I'm not going anywhere.

195
00:10:50,066 --> 00:10:51,442
[Mari chuckles]

196
00:10:55,113 --> 00:10:56,114
Would you eat?

197
00:11:05,999 --> 00:11:08,626
Mari, your curry,
it's the best in the whole world.

198
00:11:08,710 --> 00:11:10,170
[chuckles]

199
00:11:10,253 --> 00:11:11,254
It's that good?

200
00:11:11,838 --> 00:11:13,298
[Mari laughs]

201
00:11:13,381 --> 00:11:14,465
That's nice to hear.

202
00:11:15,341 --> 00:11:16,342
[chuckles]

203
00:11:17,135 --> 00:11:19,053
It's amazing. [chuckles]

204
00:11:31,107 --> 00:11:32,609
DEAR KARIN SHIRAHAMA,
CONGRATULATIONS

205
00:11:32,692 --> 00:11:35,403
ON TAKING FIRST PLACE
AT GREEN NOVA CORPORATION FESTA.

206
00:11:35,486 --> 00:11:37,947
THESE ARE THE DETAILS

207
00:11:41,409 --> 00:11:43,411
[♪ pensive music playing]

208
00:11:47,123 --> 00:11:48,541
ARTICLE 9. THE GRANTEE SHALL
MAKE EVERY EFFORT

209
00:11:48,625 --> 00:11:50,335
TO MAINTAIN THE CERTIFIED PRODUCE
AT THE SAME QUALITY…

210
00:11:50,418 --> 00:11:54,672
You know I understand your dedication
to preserving top notch quality.

211
00:11:56,090 --> 00:11:58,968
However, remember that choosing one thing

212
00:11:59,510 --> 00:12:03,264
often means that another thing
will inevitably fall to the wayside.

213
00:12:09,020 --> 00:12:10,313
MORNING:
OVERNIGHT MOISTURE RETENTION

214
00:12:10,396 --> 00:12:12,273
NOON-MIDDAY: FIRMNESS
TEMPORARILY DECREASES

215
00:12:26,955 --> 00:12:29,707
Yep. Better listen
to my gut about this one.

216
00:12:48,810 --> 00:12:52,063
I SINCERELY APPRECIATE
YOUR PROPOSAL FOR A BRANDING DEAL.

217
00:12:52,146 --> 00:12:55,733
AFTER CAREFUL CONSIDERATION, I HAVE
DECIDED TO DECLINE THIS OFFER AT THIS TIME

218
00:13:01,155 --> 00:13:03,866
I SINCERELY APOLOGIZE
FOR HAVING TO DECLINE YOUR OFFER

219
00:13:03,950 --> 00:13:05,493
SHIRAHAMA
SEND

220
00:13:06,619 --> 00:13:07,620
[sighs]

221
00:13:15,044 --> 00:13:16,212
Hmm.

222
00:13:31,519 --> 00:13:34,230
[announcer on PA] <i>Attention,</i>
<i>all passengers who wish to disembark,</i>

223
00:13:34,314 --> 00:13:37,358
<i>please follow the crew's instructions</i>
<i>and exit one at a time.</i>

224
00:13:37,442 --> 00:13:40,153
<i>Watch your step while exiting,</i>
<i>and please make sure</i>

225
00:13:40,236 --> 00:13:42,947
<i>that you have all the belongings</i>
<i>you brought onto the ferry with you</i>

226
00:13:43,031 --> 00:13:44,240
<i>before you disembark.</i>

227
00:13:44,741 --> 00:13:45,742
Kunam, over here!

228
00:13:45,825 --> 00:13:49,245
[announcer]<i> …our ferry service, and</i>
<i>we hope you enjoy the rest of your day.</i>

229
00:13:54,459 --> 00:13:56,085
What a long day.

230
00:13:56,669 --> 00:13:59,005
Mari, I'm sorry I've kept you waiting.

231
00:13:59,088 --> 00:14:00,715
Mm-mmm, no worries.

232
00:14:01,966 --> 00:14:03,718
More importantly,

233
00:14:05,136 --> 00:14:06,387
how do you think it went?

234
00:14:10,892 --> 00:14:12,268
I'm guessing no luck?

235
00:14:17,148 --> 00:14:20,902
[chuckles] Turn that frown upside down!
You've got plenty of time to sort it out.

236
00:14:20,985 --> 00:14:24,280
Besides, I heard that particular company
isn't all that great anyway.

237
00:14:24,363 --> 00:14:25,948
You don't have
to accept an offer from them.

238
00:14:26,032 --> 00:14:28,409
Oh, do you really think that?

239
00:14:28,493 --> 00:14:29,494
Mm-hmm.

240
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:33,081
[sighs] What should I do then?

241
00:14:34,332 --> 00:14:36,417
Because that company gave me

242
00:14:36,501 --> 00:14:39,337
- a job offer!
- [squeals]

243
00:14:39,420 --> 00:14:42,173
You're kidding! Congratulations! [giggles]

244
00:14:42,256 --> 00:14:44,509
You totally had me fooled, Kunam!

245
00:14:45,259 --> 00:14:47,929
I really wanted it to be a surprise.
I'm sorry, Mari.

246
00:14:48,012 --> 00:14:50,264
[laughs] This is such a surprise.

247
00:14:50,348 --> 00:14:51,849
WE HAVE DECIDED TO MOVE FORWARD
WITH YOUR APPLICATION

248
00:14:51,933 --> 00:14:52,934
This is for real, for real!

249
00:14:53,017 --> 00:14:55,728
[gasps] Does this mean you don't
have to go back to Korea anymore?

250
00:14:55,812 --> 00:14:57,772
- Mm-hmm.
- [gasps]

251
00:15:04,153 --> 00:15:05,154
I brought you a flower.

252
00:15:05,988 --> 00:15:07,615
[giggles]

253
00:15:07,698 --> 00:15:09,367
Oh, thank you.

254
00:15:09,450 --> 00:15:12,620
Mari, it must've been so hard
to wait so long for me.

255
00:15:17,500 --> 00:15:19,168
I'm proud of you, Kunam.

256
00:15:19,669 --> 00:15:22,004
You've worked so hard for this.

257
00:15:22,588 --> 00:15:23,923
Not more than you.

258
00:15:26,342 --> 00:15:29,011
- [giggles]
- [Kunam exclaims]

259
00:15:29,095 --> 00:15:31,389
- [chuckles]
- [Mari] You did it! [chuckles]

260
00:15:31,472 --> 00:15:33,182
- Awesome!
- Awesome!

261
00:15:40,731 --> 00:15:42,608
- [Kunam] Boss.
- [chuckles]

262
00:15:43,234 --> 00:15:46,445
Kunam. I heard your news
through the grapevine.

263
00:15:46,529 --> 00:15:47,572
[both chuckle]

264
00:15:47,655 --> 00:15:50,032
I appreciate everything
you've done for me here.

265
00:15:51,534 --> 00:15:52,994
That really means a lot to me.

266
00:15:53,578 --> 00:15:54,912
I'm happy for you, Kunam.

267
00:15:55,496 --> 00:15:57,456
But I'll admit
it's gonna be a little lonely

268
00:15:57,540 --> 00:15:59,834
without seeing your face
around here every day.

269
00:15:59,917 --> 00:16:02,628
Even still, I'm really proud of you, kid.

270
00:16:02,712 --> 00:16:04,714
I'll still come by sometimes.

271
00:16:05,798 --> 00:16:07,884
If you ever need
a helping hand, or anything,

272
00:16:07,967 --> 00:16:10,011
please don't hesitate to give me a call.

273
00:16:10,094 --> 00:16:11,596
Thanks. [chuckles]

274
00:16:11,679 --> 00:16:12,722
Oh…

275
00:16:16,184 --> 00:16:17,310
Hmm.

276
00:16:19,604 --> 00:16:21,814
For you. To congratulate you.

277
00:16:34,368 --> 00:16:36,787
You know,
back when I was a young buck like you,

278
00:16:36,871 --> 00:16:40,124
I worked at a big company
with a fancy tie around my neck.

279
00:16:40,208 --> 00:16:41,876
[♪ gentle music playing]

280
00:16:41,959 --> 00:16:44,921
There was a time
when I thought being successful

281
00:16:45,004 --> 00:16:46,797
was just about making money.

282
00:16:47,298 --> 00:16:51,469
Working there helped me figure out
how to stand on my own two feet.

283
00:16:52,428 --> 00:16:57,016
A workplace isn't just somewhere people go
to clock in, work, and clock out.

284
00:16:58,142 --> 00:17:01,020
It's a place where ya learn
what your strengths are,

285
00:17:01,103 --> 00:17:02,772
figure out how to apply yourself.

286
00:17:04,899 --> 00:17:07,777
If there's anything I know to be true,
it's this…

287
00:17:07,860 --> 00:17:09,403
my Kunam will be great!

288
00:17:11,739 --> 00:17:13,115
Thank you so much, sir.

289
00:17:14,617 --> 00:17:16,619
I will wear this with pride.

290
00:17:17,787 --> 00:17:19,622
Mm-hmm. [chuckles]

291
00:17:20,665 --> 00:17:22,166
[chuckles]

292
00:17:45,439 --> 00:17:46,816
[sighs]

293
00:17:50,736 --> 00:17:51,988
[grunts]

294
00:18:15,344 --> 00:18:16,929
[sighs, chuckles]

295
00:18:18,764 --> 00:18:19,765
[sighs]

296
00:18:21,267 --> 00:18:22,768
YUBIN'S SKETCHBOOK

297
00:18:22,852 --> 00:18:25,229
[in Korean] Wow…
When did she even make this?

298
00:18:53,341 --> 00:18:55,843
CERTIFICATE OF APPRECIATION
MR. MASATO KUROKAWA

299
00:19:07,438 --> 00:19:09,398
- [knock on door]
- [in English] Come in.

300
00:19:10,566 --> 00:19:11,567
Pardon me, sir.

301
00:19:16,072 --> 00:19:18,866
Ultimately,
Shirahama Karin declined the offer.

302
00:19:18,949 --> 00:19:20,701
[♪ interesting music playing]

303
00:19:20,785 --> 00:19:21,952
[inhales sharply]

304
00:19:27,958 --> 00:19:30,795
[secretary] Now, regarding the matter
you requested me to look into…

305
00:19:34,757 --> 00:19:36,592
He's a Korean named Lee Yubin.

306
00:19:38,094 --> 00:19:39,470
Hmm.

307
00:19:39,553 --> 00:19:40,721
What else?

308
00:19:40,805 --> 00:19:42,765
He's lauded as a top spatial designer.

309
00:19:43,474 --> 00:19:44,725
Spatial designer?

310
00:19:44,809 --> 00:19:45,810
Yes.

311
00:19:48,145 --> 00:19:52,483
Why is a Korean spatial designer
butting his nose into Karin's business?

312
00:19:54,485 --> 00:19:58,447
Well, it seems, sir, that his father
left him some land on Charo Island.

313
00:20:00,950 --> 00:20:03,619
[inhales sharply]
Yubin is Lee Gyeongsu's son.

314
00:20:03,703 --> 00:20:05,538
[♪ dramatic music playing]

315
00:20:11,043 --> 00:20:12,503
Of course he is…

316
00:20:14,004 --> 00:20:16,090
No wonder he rubs me the wrong way.

317
00:20:36,318 --> 00:20:37,445
[taps on desk]

318
00:20:47,997 --> 00:20:49,540
[in Korean] Where are we?

319
00:20:50,583 --> 00:20:51,834
I'm scared, I'm scared.

320
00:20:51,917 --> 00:20:53,544
- [in English] I'm scared, I'm scared. Ah!
- Ah! Oh.

321
00:20:53,627 --> 00:20:56,464
[in Korean] Where are we?

322
00:20:56,547 --> 00:20:58,507
- You can take off your blindfolds.
- Huh?

323
00:20:58,591 --> 00:21:00,843
- Can I take this off now?
- [in English] Yep.

324
00:21:00,926 --> 00:21:03,095
- [villagers cheering]
- [in Korean] Oh, my gosh! What the…

325
00:21:05,097 --> 00:21:07,892
- [chuckles]
- Yubin!

326
00:21:07,975 --> 00:21:09,310
[in English] Welcome back.

327
00:21:09,393 --> 00:21:10,394
[villager 1] Yubin!

328
00:21:11,187 --> 00:21:13,230
- [villager 2] Yay!
- [in Korean] What? What's going on?

329
00:21:13,731 --> 00:21:15,149
What?

330
00:21:15,232 --> 00:21:18,861
- [in Korean] What's going on?
- [in English] This is for you. [chuckles]

331
00:21:18,944 --> 00:21:20,029
[villagers cheering, chuckling]

332
00:21:20,112 --> 00:21:21,655
CHARO YUBIN

333
00:21:21,739 --> 00:21:23,032
- [laughs]
- [all cheering]

334
00:21:23,115 --> 00:21:25,117
[villager 3] Yay! [chuckles]

335
00:21:25,201 --> 00:21:27,036
Thank you so much. What a surprise.

336
00:21:27,119 --> 00:21:29,538
It's a welcome back
to Charo Island party, Yubin.

337
00:21:30,623 --> 00:21:32,875
- This is for me? Huh?
- Mm-hmm.

338
00:21:32,958 --> 00:21:34,502
WELCOME BACK, YUBIN

339
00:21:34,585 --> 00:21:35,753
[Karin] Without your help,

340
00:21:35,836 --> 00:21:37,838
we never would have managed
to place first at the Festa.

341
00:21:38,422 --> 00:21:40,800
[villagers cheering, applauding]

342
00:21:41,300 --> 00:21:43,260
- [villager 1] Thank you.
- [villager 2] So great.

343
00:21:43,344 --> 00:21:45,095
[in Korean] Thank you.
[in English] Thank you, everyone.

344
00:21:45,179 --> 00:21:47,890
- [in Korean] Thank you.
- [in English] Yeah! You're finally back.

345
00:21:47,973 --> 00:21:49,350
Why don't we eat first?

346
00:21:49,433 --> 00:21:51,435
Oh, over here. Over here.
Sit down right here.

347
00:21:51,519 --> 00:21:53,604
- Your seat is here.
- [all clamoring]

348
00:21:54,188 --> 00:21:55,856
- Here, Yubin, over here.
- Karin, Karin.

349
00:21:55,940 --> 00:21:59,777
- But I ate a lot and I'm still so full.
- You're a strapping young man,

350
00:21:59,860 --> 00:22:02,488
- you can eat a lot more than that!
- Sit down, sit down right here.

351
00:22:03,197 --> 00:22:04,240
Come on.

352
00:22:04,949 --> 00:22:06,909
- Say "ah".
- Oh… [stammers]

353
00:22:06,992 --> 00:22:08,869
[all chattering, laughing]

354
00:22:09,787 --> 00:22:12,248
- This is delicious.
- [exclaims]

355
00:22:12,331 --> 00:22:15,918
So, don't tell us that it happened again?

356
00:22:17,294 --> 00:22:19,421
Did you fall for another scam?

357
00:22:19,505 --> 00:22:21,882
No, of course not! Leave him alone!

358
00:22:21,966 --> 00:22:23,133
- [gasps]
- Hey!

359
00:22:23,217 --> 00:22:25,302
Don't tease the poor boy, shame on you.

360
00:22:25,386 --> 00:22:27,596
You have to pretend
you don't know a thing, like I do.

361
00:22:27,680 --> 00:22:29,932
- It's a misunderstanding, Grandmas.
- [chuckles]

362
00:22:30,015 --> 00:22:31,308
[in Korean] Seriously, no.

363
00:22:31,392 --> 00:22:34,144
[in English] Well, we gotta toast
on a special day like this, right?

364
00:22:34,812 --> 00:22:36,272
- Grab your cups.
- [Karin] Oh.

365
00:22:36,355 --> 00:22:38,566
- Oh, I'll fill your glass. Get this going.
- Oh.

366
00:22:39,108 --> 00:22:42,027
- [chuckles]
- [chattering, laughing continues]

367
00:22:42,111 --> 00:22:44,697
- [Karin] Yay, thank you so much!
- [Yubin] Wow, yes, thank you.

368
00:22:44,780 --> 00:22:46,073
Yeah, that's good.

369
00:22:46,156 --> 00:22:48,868
- Thank you.
- [Karin] Oh, how kind of you, thank you.

370
00:22:48,951 --> 00:22:49,952
[chief] Yubin.

371
00:22:50,786 --> 00:22:52,621
Thanks for coming back here.
To our island.

372
00:22:52,705 --> 00:22:55,291
- Yeah. [chuckles]
- Yes.

373
00:22:55,374 --> 00:22:58,252
May Yubin's days be filled
with nothing but good fortune.

374
00:22:58,919 --> 00:23:01,213
- Everyone, cheers!
- [in Korean] Cheers!

375
00:23:01,297 --> 00:23:02,798
- [in English] Cheers!
- [villagers] Cheers!

376
00:23:02,882 --> 00:23:04,091
[exclaiming]

377
00:23:04,174 --> 00:23:06,051
[villagers] Cheers!

378
00:23:06,135 --> 00:23:09,722
[all chattering]

379
00:23:19,481 --> 00:23:20,649
[sighs]

380
00:23:24,069 --> 00:23:28,741
NEW HIRE ORIENTATION
A.K. TOURIST LTD.

381
00:23:28,824 --> 00:23:30,993
Well, it's time for us to get started.
[inhales deeply]

382
00:23:31,076 --> 00:23:33,621
I'm from A.K. Tourist's Human Resources.

383
00:23:33,704 --> 00:23:35,915
It's a pleasure to meet you all.
I'm Chiba.

384
00:23:35,998 --> 00:23:38,375
- [employees] Thank you.
- It's nice to meet you.

385
00:23:39,543 --> 00:23:43,881
As you're aware, you won't be starting
your positions for three more months,

386
00:23:43,964 --> 00:23:47,551
but we wanted to hold this orientation to
explain your responsibilities in advance.

387
00:23:47,635 --> 00:23:49,303
Well, without further ado…

388
00:23:49,386 --> 00:23:51,388
Please introduce yourselves,
one at a time,

389
00:23:51,472 --> 00:23:53,766
starting from the person in the back,
on the right.

390
00:23:54,516 --> 00:23:55,851
All right.

391
00:23:56,685 --> 00:23:58,103
My name is Sakuraba Mizuki.

392
00:23:58,771 --> 00:24:02,316
I applied here because I want to share
the joys of traveling with others.

393
00:24:02,399 --> 00:24:03,984
I look forward to working with you all.

394
00:24:04,068 --> 00:24:06,153
- [employees] It's nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you.

395
00:24:09,865 --> 00:24:12,159
Hello, everyone. My name is Park Kunam.

396
00:24:14,328 --> 00:24:16,497
Uh, I decided to apply
for this company because

397
00:24:17,331 --> 00:24:19,708
I want to make a lot of people "snile"…

398
00:24:20,584 --> 00:24:23,754
Because I want to make
a lot of people smile.

399
00:24:23,837 --> 00:24:25,464
I look forward to working with you all.

400
00:24:26,382 --> 00:24:28,342
[Chiba] So getting into it…

401
00:24:28,425 --> 00:24:31,261
We'll start by reviewing all
of the regulations you will need to know,

402
00:24:31,345 --> 00:24:35,224
regarding tourism in Japan and
the standard practices of our industry,

403
00:24:35,307 --> 00:24:38,227
as well as laws and regulations
from other countries

404
00:24:38,310 --> 00:24:40,354
that may arise
while traveling around the world.

405
00:24:40,896 --> 00:24:42,356
Good. All right.

406
00:24:42,439 --> 00:24:44,024
- Is he by himself?
- He's sitting alone.

407
00:24:44,108 --> 00:24:45,442
- Is this my chance?
- Yes, go now.

408
00:24:45,526 --> 00:24:46,986
- Should we go? Let's go.
- Let's go.

409
00:24:52,408 --> 00:24:53,909
[employee] Hi. Hello.

410
00:24:55,202 --> 00:24:56,829
You said you're Park Kunam?

411
00:24:58,080 --> 00:24:59,081
Uh, yes, hello.

412
00:24:59,164 --> 00:25:00,541
Do you mind if we sit here?

413
00:25:01,208 --> 00:25:02,710
Not at all, go ahead.

414
00:25:02,793 --> 00:25:04,712
[both chuckle]

415
00:25:04,795 --> 00:25:06,964
- I'll set this right here.
- Thanks for letting us join you.

416
00:25:07,673 --> 00:25:11,301
So, was there a reason
that you decided to work in this country?

417
00:25:11,385 --> 00:25:13,262
Have you been in Japan very long?

418
00:25:13,345 --> 00:25:16,098
- Um, well, a little bit.
- [employee chuckles]

419
00:25:16,682 --> 00:25:19,309
[villagers chattering]

420
00:25:22,396 --> 00:25:25,107
[sighs] I wonder what Kunam's doing.

421
00:25:26,608 --> 00:25:28,527
I hope he's fitting in all right.

422
00:25:28,610 --> 00:25:29,903
He's too kindhearted.

423
00:25:29,987 --> 00:25:34,324
What if the people at work bully him
because he's such a good guy? [sighs]

424
00:25:34,408 --> 00:25:38,120
Listen, this company is something
I'm very knowledgeable about.

425
00:25:38,620 --> 00:25:42,374
So if you're ever unsure about anything,
feel free to ask me okay?

426
00:25:44,001 --> 00:25:46,170
I do have one question.

427
00:25:46,253 --> 00:25:49,048
Yes. Did something pique your interest?

428
00:25:50,591 --> 00:25:52,092
Can we eat before we talk?

429
00:25:52,676 --> 00:25:54,178
I barely ate and I'm starving.

430
00:25:55,429 --> 00:25:56,430
Oh, uh…

431
00:25:57,222 --> 00:25:59,224
Right, it is our lunch hour.

432
00:25:59,308 --> 00:26:00,893
Don't mind us at all.

433
00:26:00,976 --> 00:26:02,311
[phone buzzes]

434
00:26:05,773 --> 00:26:08,650
[Mari] <i>Hi, Kunam!</i>
<i>Can you call me when you have a minute?</i>

435
00:26:08,734 --> 00:26:11,111
<i>Just for a second. I miss your voice.</i>

436
00:26:12,112 --> 00:26:13,363
Enjoy your lunch.

437
00:26:14,573 --> 00:26:15,657
Mari, hi.

438
00:26:16,784 --> 00:26:17,826
Yep.

439
00:26:19,036 --> 00:26:20,621
Mmm…

440
00:26:21,747 --> 00:26:24,458
It sounds like
you're fitting in just great.

441
00:26:25,667 --> 00:26:28,378
Ah. Mari, can I call you back later?

442
00:26:28,921 --> 00:26:30,547
I have to head back in,
my lunch break's over.

443
00:26:30,631 --> 00:26:31,673
Mmm.

444
00:26:32,591 --> 00:26:33,592
Hey.

445
00:26:34,384 --> 00:26:37,221
You better not let your eyes wander
to anybody at your company.

446
00:26:37,805 --> 00:26:39,431
I'm practically invisible here.

447
00:26:40,224 --> 00:26:42,392
<i>- I'll talk to you later.</i>
- Mm-hmm.

448
00:26:49,233 --> 00:26:50,609
[sighs, chuckles]

449
00:26:54,738 --> 00:26:57,741
[sighs, speaks Korean] Working
for a company is really exhausting.

450
00:27:02,287 --> 00:27:04,206
- [in English] Well, look who it is.
- [gasps]

451
00:27:04,289 --> 00:27:06,959
Where'd you come from?
Why are you here, Mari?

452
00:27:07,042 --> 00:27:09,586
Did you forget I said
that I would meet you here?

453
00:27:09,670 --> 00:27:11,004
We haven't had a date in a while.

454
00:27:12,923 --> 00:27:15,884
- [♪ playful music playing]
- [sighs]

455
00:27:15,968 --> 00:27:18,428
Is something wrong?
Why do you look like that?

456
00:27:20,472 --> 00:27:22,182
It was such a long day.

457
00:27:23,267 --> 00:27:25,561
I don't know half the terms
they use at this place.

458
00:27:26,645 --> 00:27:29,106
[chuckles] Well, good thing it's over now.

459
00:27:30,190 --> 00:27:33,777
I'll cook you so much yummy food
that you'll forget how hard your day was.

460
00:27:33,861 --> 00:27:35,904
[both chuckling]

461
00:27:39,032 --> 00:27:40,617
- Oh. Oh.
- Oh.

462
00:27:40,701 --> 00:27:42,536
- It's raining.
- It's gonna pour.

463
00:27:42,619 --> 00:27:44,121
- Want my jacket?
- Huh?

464
00:27:46,290 --> 00:27:47,499
Don't wanna get sick.

465
00:27:50,252 --> 00:27:51,253
Let's run, okay?

466
00:27:52,087 --> 00:27:53,755
- Uh-huh. [chuckles]
- [chuckles]

467
00:27:55,507 --> 00:27:58,844
- [Kunam] Come on. Faster, faster!
- [Mari] Hurry, Kunam! Run!

468
00:28:03,974 --> 00:28:07,144
[in Korean] Wow.
The weather's just perfect.

469
00:28:10,147 --> 00:28:11,481
[sighs]

470
00:28:12,566 --> 00:28:16,194
In any case, what can I do on this island?

471
00:28:17,946 --> 00:28:19,740
What now? Man…

472
00:28:21,533 --> 00:28:22,951
[sighs]

473
00:28:25,662 --> 00:28:26,914
[bell rings]

474
00:28:30,042 --> 00:28:31,418
[in English] Chief, over here!

475
00:28:32,544 --> 00:28:33,921
Hi, Chief!

476
00:28:34,922 --> 00:28:37,633
- [laughs] Hi, Yubin!
- [chuckles]

477
00:28:37,716 --> 00:28:39,217
Just who I was looking for.

478
00:28:39,301 --> 00:28:41,762
[♪ pop music playing]

479
00:28:41,845 --> 00:28:42,971
CHIEF'S BIKE

480
00:28:43,055 --> 00:28:45,515
[in Korean] Where should I go?

481
00:28:45,599 --> 00:28:47,726
[exclaims]

482
00:28:48,352 --> 00:28:49,853
- [in English] Grandmas?
- [both gasp]

483
00:28:49,937 --> 00:28:51,730
- Look, Yubin's here.
- Yubin.

484
00:28:51,813 --> 00:28:53,315
Do you need help with that?

485
00:28:53,398 --> 00:28:56,318
- This pump's givin' us a lot of trouble.
- Oh, no, it is?

486
00:28:56,401 --> 00:28:58,320
[Grandma] Look, this isn't doing
what it's supposed to do.

487
00:28:58,403 --> 00:29:00,822
- I keep pumping but it's not working.
- Let me look at it. Huh?

488
00:29:01,615 --> 00:29:03,784
[in Korean] Oh. Is it broken?

489
00:29:03,867 --> 00:29:05,619
- Oh? Ah!
- [in English] What is it?

490
00:29:06,244 --> 00:29:07,788
- Ah, okay.
- Hmm?

491
00:29:08,288 --> 00:29:10,415
- It should work correctly now. [grunts]
- Really?

492
00:29:11,208 --> 00:29:13,710
- [both exclaiming]
- [exclaims] All right.

493
00:29:13,794 --> 00:29:17,631
Oh! Amazing! Yes, thank you.
You're wonderful.

494
00:29:17,714 --> 00:29:19,216
- Do you need any more help?
- Thank you.

495
00:29:19,299 --> 00:29:21,760
Oh, we have a lot more to fix.
It's an old house.

496
00:29:21,843 --> 00:29:23,512
- A lot, a lot? Huh?
- Come inside with us.

497
00:29:23,595 --> 00:29:24,888
- While you're here…
- Uh-huh.

498
00:29:24,972 --> 00:29:26,932
- …why don't you join us for lunch?
- For lunch?

499
00:29:27,015 --> 00:29:28,392
- Yes, lunch!
- How much will I owe you?

500
00:29:28,475 --> 00:29:30,435
- Lunch is free, and it's delicious.
- It's free? Free is the best!

501
00:29:30,519 --> 00:29:32,938
Chiyo, you're invited too,
let's go inside!

502
00:29:38,151 --> 00:29:40,028
[brakes screech]

503
00:29:48,912 --> 00:29:50,288
[sighs]

504
00:29:59,047 --> 00:30:02,592
[gasps] Oh, my goodness.
All the flowers are in full bloom again.

505
00:30:02,676 --> 00:30:05,220
[exclaims, chuckles]

506
00:30:06,972 --> 00:30:08,849
[children chattering]

507
00:30:12,102 --> 00:30:13,270
Oh…

508
00:30:14,062 --> 00:30:15,188
[in Korean] Here you go.

509
00:30:20,485 --> 00:30:22,279
- Huh?
- [in English] Can you play with us.

510
00:30:22,362 --> 00:30:23,655
You want me?

511
00:30:24,531 --> 00:30:25,657
[in Korean] Okay.

512
00:30:26,199 --> 00:30:28,827
- Let's go! Run!
- [children exclaiming]

513
00:30:28,910 --> 00:30:31,663
- [exclaims] Over here.
- [exclaiming continues]

514
00:30:31,747 --> 00:30:33,373
[in English] Pass, pass.

515
00:30:33,999 --> 00:30:35,208
[in Korean] Got it!

516
00:30:35,917 --> 00:30:37,002
[exclaims]

517
00:30:43,216 --> 00:30:44,885
- [in English] Grandpa Asahi!
- [Asahi] Yubin.

518
00:30:44,968 --> 00:30:47,345
- [exclaims] Let me handle it, I got it.
- Oh, ah…

519
00:30:47,429 --> 00:30:49,973
- Here.
- It's too much trouble for you, Yubin.

520
00:30:50,557 --> 00:30:52,059
- Over here?
- That's great.

521
00:30:53,226 --> 00:30:55,145
[Asahi grunts]

522
00:30:56,813 --> 00:30:58,106
- I'm all finished.
- [Asahi] Oh…

523
00:30:58,190 --> 00:30:59,524
SURFBOARD RENTAL
SURFING SET RENTAL

524
00:30:59,608 --> 00:31:00,692
[gasps] Wow.

525
00:31:00,776 --> 00:31:03,612
I can't thank you enough!
How generous of you to help.

526
00:31:03,695 --> 00:31:07,157
- Oh. <i>Gamsa… habnida</i>.
- Ah, <i>gamsahabnida</i>.

527
00:31:07,240 --> 00:31:08,450
[in English] You're most welcome.

528
00:31:08,533 --> 00:31:09,910
Here, here's a little gift!

529
00:31:09,993 --> 00:31:12,537
- Huh? What is it?
- That's just a little treat.

530
00:31:12,621 --> 00:31:13,622
- A little treat?
- Yeah.

531
00:31:13,705 --> 00:31:15,165
You're giving this to me for free?

532
00:31:15,248 --> 00:31:16,666
- On the house. Yep.
- It's free. I don't have to pay?

533
00:31:16,750 --> 00:31:18,126
- All yours for free.
- Oh, I love free things.

534
00:31:18,210 --> 00:31:19,711
And I love you! Thank you for this!

535
00:31:19,795 --> 00:31:21,421
Good. I love you too, ya rascal!

536
00:31:21,505 --> 00:31:22,923
- Grandpa Asahi…
- Yeah?

537
00:31:23,423 --> 00:31:24,549
I love you!

538
00:31:24,633 --> 00:31:26,009
[Asahi exclaims]

539
00:31:26,093 --> 00:31:27,344
Love ya back!

540
00:31:29,221 --> 00:31:32,432
- [chief] Yubin, over here. [laughs]
- Oh, Chief. Chief!

541
00:31:32,516 --> 00:31:34,184
- [villager 1] Yubin!
- [Yubin] Hi, Grandma!

542
00:31:34,267 --> 00:31:36,812
- [villager 2] You're the sweetest!
- [Yubin] Whoa! Yes, coming!

543
00:31:36,895 --> 00:31:38,814
I'll be right there!

544
00:31:38,897 --> 00:31:40,440
I'm on my way!

545
00:31:42,609 --> 00:31:43,777
- Good evening.
- [child 1] Hello.

546
00:31:43,860 --> 00:31:44,861
[children] Good evening.

547
00:31:47,405 --> 00:31:48,782
[screaming]

548
00:31:48,865 --> 00:31:50,575
- [child 2] This is scary!
- [child 1] It's so dark!

549
00:31:50,659 --> 00:31:52,410
Tunnel monster!

550
00:31:52,494 --> 00:31:54,121
[child 2 exclaims] I'm so glad we're out!

551
00:31:54,204 --> 00:31:55,580
[child 3] We didn't get eaten.

552
00:31:55,664 --> 00:31:57,124
[child 2 panting]

553
00:32:00,127 --> 00:32:02,295
[lightbulb crackling]

554
00:32:03,171 --> 00:32:04,172
Ah.

555
00:32:04,923 --> 00:32:06,049
[sighs]

556
00:32:09,469 --> 00:32:10,470
[in Korean] All done.

557
00:32:18,311 --> 00:32:19,312
[Yubin] Ah.

558
00:32:21,064 --> 00:32:23,066
[grunting]

559
00:32:23,150 --> 00:32:24,151
[in English] I'm back!

560
00:32:25,277 --> 00:32:27,070
I haven't seen you all day long.

561
00:32:28,029 --> 00:32:29,614
[groans] Tell me about it.

562
00:32:30,490 --> 00:32:31,491
[sighs deeply]

563
00:32:31,575 --> 00:32:33,994
I'm not working,
and yet I have so much work.

564
00:32:34,578 --> 00:32:36,496
- [giggles]
- [chuckles]

565
00:32:37,038 --> 00:32:38,206
[in Korean] I know.

566
00:32:39,374 --> 00:32:41,293
[in English] This is… Oh, wait one sec.

567
00:32:41,376 --> 00:32:43,044
- Today's pay…
- Mmm.

568
00:32:43,128 --> 00:32:44,796
- …is in this bag… right here.
- Hmm.

569
00:32:44,880 --> 00:32:46,381
- Hmm! What's in it?
- Ah.

570
00:32:47,007 --> 00:32:48,925
- Well…
- [chuckles]

571
00:32:49,009 --> 00:32:50,010
What is this?

572
00:32:50,510 --> 00:32:52,220
Did Grandpa Asahi give you this

573
00:32:52,304 --> 00:32:53,555
- for a job well done?
- Yeah.

574
00:32:53,638 --> 00:32:54,890
- I'm so hungry I could die.
- [exclaims]

575
00:32:54,973 --> 00:32:56,975
- Let's get dinner going.
- [in Korean] Let's go.

576
00:32:57,058 --> 00:32:58,518
[both chuckle]

577
00:33:02,147 --> 00:33:04,566
- [Yubin, in Korean] Uh-oh. I'm late.
- [in English] Oh, Yubin, Yubin.

578
00:33:04,649 --> 00:33:06,234
- Here. Drink some water.
- Mmm. Ah.

579
00:33:06,318 --> 00:33:07,319
- Drink up.
- Thanks.

580
00:33:08,612 --> 00:33:10,989
- [in Korean] Thanks. Hmm?
- [in English] Don't go yet.

581
00:33:11,072 --> 00:33:12,240
[in Korean] Oh. Right, right.

582
00:33:13,950 --> 00:33:15,285
- [in English] Have a great day.
- Mmm.

583
00:33:17,662 --> 00:33:19,539
- [in Korean] One more time.
- [chuckles]

584
00:33:20,790 --> 00:33:21,791
[Yubin chuckles]

585
00:33:22,584 --> 00:33:23,960
[in English] Careful out there!

586
00:33:24,753 --> 00:33:25,879
- [in Korean] See you later.
- Mm-hmm.

587
00:33:30,050 --> 00:33:32,886
[sighs, speaks in English]
I'm glad that Yubin's fitting in so well.

588
00:33:33,970 --> 00:33:36,223
Wonder if he'll get elected
to town leadership.

589
00:33:37,307 --> 00:33:38,391
[in Korean] All right.

590
00:33:39,893 --> 00:33:41,102
[in English] I'm here!

591
00:33:41,603 --> 00:33:44,231
- Oh… Right over here, Yubin.
- [Yubin exclaims, pants]

592
00:33:44,314 --> 00:33:48,026
- Whoa, whoa. Be careful up there.
- Hurry and help give me a hand over here.

593
00:33:48,109 --> 00:33:49,945
This isn't something I can fix on my own.

594
00:33:50,904 --> 00:33:51,905
[Yubin sighs]

595
00:33:53,490 --> 00:33:54,491
Okay.

596
00:33:55,242 --> 00:33:56,910
- [chief laughs]
- [Yubin grunts]

597
00:33:57,869 --> 00:33:59,412
- [groans]
- [chief laughs]

598
00:34:01,039 --> 00:34:03,208
- [Yubin groans]
- [chief chuckles]

599
00:34:04,167 --> 00:34:05,502
[groans, speaks in Korean] Let's go!

600
00:34:06,086 --> 00:34:08,421
[in English] Did you know
that Mr. Gyeongsu put this here?

601
00:34:10,340 --> 00:34:14,052
He told me that he dreamed of
pushing his son on this swing,

602
00:34:14,135 --> 00:34:15,720
someday when he came to visit.

603
00:34:18,139 --> 00:34:21,142
Actually, he always talked about
building a house here on Charo Island.

604
00:34:23,228 --> 00:34:25,230
- A house?
- Mmm. That's right.

605
00:34:26,606 --> 00:34:28,566
He talked about bringing his family.

606
00:34:28,650 --> 00:34:31,361
He planned to build a house
with a big window and an attic.

607
00:34:31,444 --> 00:34:33,280
And come to live here permanently.

608
00:34:36,241 --> 00:34:38,576
[♪ sentimental music playing]

609
00:34:42,580 --> 00:34:44,499
I was curious so I asked him,

610
00:34:44,582 --> 00:34:47,502
"Why build one out on a small island,
and not in the city?"

611
00:34:48,878 --> 00:34:51,631
Once he explained it to me,
it made a lot of sense.

612
00:34:51,715 --> 00:34:53,049
His wife wasn't well.

613
00:34:54,092 --> 00:34:57,012
Said the fresh island air
is just what she needed to get better.

614
00:34:58,847 --> 00:35:01,224
I can still see him
with that big smile he'd get

615
00:35:01,766 --> 00:35:04,102
whenever he'd talk about
bringing his family here.

616
00:35:04,728 --> 00:35:07,147
- It's a darn shame.
- [sighs]

617
00:35:07,230 --> 00:35:08,982
You just can't predict the future.

618
00:35:09,566 --> 00:35:11,067
Never know what can go wrong.

619
00:35:12,068 --> 00:35:13,111
[sighs]

620
00:35:17,616 --> 00:35:20,201
Well, I gotta bounce.

621
00:35:20,994 --> 00:35:23,163
There's still a bunch of things
that need to be fixed.

622
00:35:23,246 --> 00:35:24,247
[chuckles]

623
00:35:27,584 --> 00:35:28,585
[sighs]

624
00:35:38,219 --> 00:35:39,220
[sighs]

625
00:35:40,055 --> 00:35:41,056
[chuckles]

626
00:35:42,641 --> 00:35:43,642
[sighs]

627
00:35:46,269 --> 00:35:47,896
[chuckles]

628
00:35:58,740 --> 00:35:59,908
[grunts]

629
00:36:09,417 --> 00:36:10,502
[sighs]

630
00:36:31,606 --> 00:36:32,691
[sighs]

631
00:36:33,900 --> 00:36:35,151
[sighs] Wow.

632
00:36:36,569 --> 00:36:39,656
I'm glad Chief remembered that
about your dad.

633
00:36:41,199 --> 00:36:42,367
Mmm.

634
00:36:44,744 --> 00:36:45,745
[sighs]

635
00:36:46,663 --> 00:36:47,956
It was really nice to hear.

636
00:36:49,582 --> 00:36:51,042
I realized…

637
00:36:52,085 --> 00:36:53,336
I'm still just a kid…

638
00:36:55,422 --> 00:36:56,423
with a lot to learn.

639
00:36:57,590 --> 00:36:58,591
Mm-mmm.

640
00:37:05,181 --> 00:37:06,182
Well…

641
00:37:06,683 --> 00:37:07,809
Now it's your turn.

642
00:37:07,892 --> 00:37:08,893
Tell me everything.

643
00:37:08,977 --> 00:37:10,854
- Hmm?
- How was your day?

644
00:37:11,354 --> 00:37:12,522
- Oh, my day?
- Mmm.

645
00:37:15,483 --> 00:37:16,651
Mmm…

646
00:37:17,986 --> 00:37:19,571
- Tomorrow…
- Mmm.

647
00:37:20,321 --> 00:37:21,573
Remember I told you

648
00:37:21,656 --> 00:37:23,742
- we would be distributing…
- Mmm.

649
00:37:23,825 --> 00:37:26,494
- …the island's produce through Green Nova?
- Yeah.

650
00:37:27,078 --> 00:37:30,290
Well, tomorrow is supposed to be
the first day. It finally starts.

651
00:37:30,373 --> 00:37:31,624
Ah, that's right.

652
00:37:32,459 --> 00:37:34,419
That's why everyone was so busy today.

653
00:37:34,502 --> 00:37:35,754
Mm-hmm. Yep.

654
00:37:35,837 --> 00:37:36,838
[Yubin] Mmm.

655
00:37:37,338 --> 00:37:38,673
That's why… [sighs]

656
00:37:40,216 --> 00:37:41,968
- I'm a tiny bit…
- Mmm?

657
00:37:43,636 --> 00:37:44,804
I'm a little nervous.

658
00:37:44,888 --> 00:37:46,931
- Hmm? You are?
- Mm-hmm.

659
00:37:47,015 --> 00:37:48,099
There's nothing to worry about.

660
00:37:48,183 --> 00:37:50,393
- [in Korean] Don't worry.
- Hmm.

661
00:37:50,477 --> 00:37:52,061
You'll be just fine.

662
00:37:52,145 --> 00:37:53,646
[♪ tender music playing]

663
00:37:54,355 --> 00:37:55,356
Mmm.

664
00:37:55,440 --> 00:37:57,692
- You'll be just fine.
- Mm-hmm.

665
00:37:58,902 --> 00:38:00,320
[sighing] You'll be just fine.

666
00:38:02,071 --> 00:38:04,741
- Drink your hot chocolate.
- Hmm?

667
00:38:04,824 --> 00:38:06,534
Blow your nerves away.

668
00:38:08,995 --> 00:38:09,996
[cups clink]

669
00:38:14,667 --> 00:38:15,668
[Yubin sighs] Mmm.

670
00:38:16,961 --> 00:38:17,962
[sighs]

671
00:38:19,506 --> 00:38:20,924
[in English] My stomach's in knots.

672
00:38:22,300 --> 00:38:23,551
Don't worry.

673
00:38:23,635 --> 00:38:24,719
[chuckles]

674
00:38:24,803 --> 00:38:26,638
SOLD

675
00:38:29,474 --> 00:38:30,725
- Um, excuse me.
- Yes?

676
00:38:30,809 --> 00:38:33,728
I'd like to pick up my usual order
for organic fertilizer.

677
00:38:33,812 --> 00:38:35,688
Oh… My apologies.

678
00:38:35,772 --> 00:38:37,607
We don't have any stock in store
at the moment.

679
00:38:38,191 --> 00:38:40,318
You ran out of stock?
You always have a lot.

680
00:38:40,401 --> 00:38:41,736
Right, but…

681
00:38:41,820 --> 00:38:46,199
Green Nova Corporation has single-handedly
purchased all of our inventory.

682
00:38:46,282 --> 00:38:49,828
NURSERY SOIL SOLD
TO GREEN NOVA CORPORATION LTD

683
00:38:49,911 --> 00:38:50,912
Oh.

684
00:38:51,496 --> 00:38:53,248
When does your next shipment come in?

685
00:38:53,331 --> 00:38:54,332
[clerk sighs]

686
00:38:54,415 --> 00:38:56,376
That information's not available yet.

687
00:38:56,459 --> 00:38:57,752
Apologies for the inconvenience.

688
00:39:04,008 --> 00:39:07,846
THANK YOU FOR YOUR PURCHASE
SOLD - GREEN NOVA CORPORATION LTD.

689
00:39:07,929 --> 00:39:10,306
- They're late.
- Yeah, they're late. Yep.

690
00:39:10,390 --> 00:39:11,850
Pretty sure they said
they were coming at 9 a.m.

691
00:39:11,933 --> 00:39:13,309
KARIN'S SWEET POTATOES

692
00:39:13,393 --> 00:39:14,394
What could be taking 'em so long?

693
00:39:14,477 --> 00:39:15,770
SPECIAL SELECTION
KABOCHA PUMPKINS

694
00:39:15,854 --> 00:39:17,105
- Are you sure?
- [chief] Oh.

695
00:39:17,188 --> 00:39:20,024
What the heck is this nonsense?
Why are they so late?

696
00:39:20,108 --> 00:39:21,109
[villagers chattering]

697
00:39:21,192 --> 00:39:23,611
- What's going on?
- They shoulda been here a good while ago.

698
00:39:23,695 --> 00:39:25,530
- What?
- They're really late.

699
00:39:25,613 --> 00:39:28,157
- Can you give 'em a call?
- Sure, I'm gonna call right now.

700
00:39:28,241 --> 00:39:30,618
- [villager] What's going on?
- [villagers continue chattering]

701
00:39:31,619 --> 00:39:33,037
[line ringing]

702
00:39:36,749 --> 00:39:37,750
Hello? Can you help me?

703
00:39:37,834 --> 00:39:40,086
I'm calling from Charo Island.
This is Shirahama Karin.

704
00:39:40,169 --> 00:39:41,963
There's a pick-up scheduled for today.

705
00:39:42,046 --> 00:39:44,173
We're standing by,
waiting for the truck to arrive.

706
00:39:44,257 --> 00:39:45,466
When should we be expecting it?

707
00:39:45,550 --> 00:39:49,053
[worker] <i>Uh, Charo Island isn't included</i>
<i>in our list of scheduled stops…</i>

708
00:39:49,137 --> 00:39:51,055
What? We're not on your list of stops?

709
00:39:52,015 --> 00:39:53,016
What?

710
00:39:53,099 --> 00:39:54,183
[villagers chattering]

711
00:39:54,267 --> 00:39:55,852
[Karin] There must've been
a misunderstanding.

712
00:39:55,935 --> 00:39:57,687
The shipment was supposed to be today.

713
00:39:57,770 --> 00:40:00,607
<i>Our operations follow</i>
<i>Green Nova Corporation's order schedule,</i>

714
00:40:00,690 --> 00:40:04,235
<i>but our records don't indicate</i>
<i>a stop at Charo Island at all.</i>

715
00:40:04,319 --> 00:40:06,446
<i>- I'm sorry for the inconvenience.</i>
- Wait. Wait, but…

716
00:40:06,946 --> 00:40:08,281
they said we'd start this month--

717
00:40:08,364 --> 00:40:09,365
[call disconnects]

718
00:40:11,034 --> 00:40:13,244
- [villager 1] I don't know…
- [villager 2] Oh, no.

719
00:40:13,328 --> 00:40:15,121
What on earth is happening?

720
00:40:15,663 --> 00:40:17,457
We grew all these vegetables with care.

721
00:40:17,540 --> 00:40:20,001
What if they go bad?
What are they gonna do about it?

722
00:40:20,084 --> 00:40:21,210
[Karin sighs]

723
00:40:21,294 --> 00:40:23,463
It looks like there was
a little miscommunication.

724
00:40:23,546 --> 00:40:25,548
Don't worry too much.
We'll figure something out.

725
00:40:25,632 --> 00:40:27,467
- [villagers groan]
- [Karin] Okay?

726
00:40:27,550 --> 00:40:29,302
- Yeah, we have to trust her.
- Okay.

727
00:40:29,385 --> 00:40:30,470
[chief] Karin.

728
00:40:30,553 --> 00:40:33,056
Can you ask Mr. Kurokawa
without alerting everyone to it?

729
00:40:33,640 --> 00:40:35,725
Since he's high up
at Green Nova Corporation,

730
00:40:35,808 --> 00:40:37,560
maybe there's a chance
he knows something about it.

731
00:40:37,644 --> 00:40:38,645
[sighs]

732
00:40:39,187 --> 00:40:40,396
That's a good idea.

733
00:40:41,189 --> 00:40:43,274
I'll go right away and ask him in person.

734
00:40:43,358 --> 00:40:45,818
- Sorry about all this.
- [villagers chattering]

735
00:40:45,902 --> 00:40:49,530
Um, everyone. I'll call you immediately
as soon as I find out more information.

736
00:40:49,614 --> 00:40:51,574
I'm sorry for all the trouble
this is causing.

737
00:40:52,241 --> 00:40:53,368
See you later.

738
00:40:53,451 --> 00:40:54,619
[villagers mumbling]

739
00:40:55,578 --> 00:40:57,622
I've done everything
in my power to impede them.

740
00:40:59,457 --> 00:41:02,043
[♪ sinister music playing]

741
00:41:06,756 --> 00:41:10,510
KUROKAWA

742
00:41:13,304 --> 00:41:14,639
What's the reason for your visit?

743
00:41:15,515 --> 00:41:17,433
I'm here to speak with Mr. Kurokawa.

744
00:41:18,601 --> 00:41:19,602
And your name is what?

745
00:41:19,686 --> 00:41:21,771
Right. My name is Shirahama Karin.

746
00:41:26,067 --> 00:41:27,068
[sighs]

747
00:41:42,417 --> 00:41:43,543
[in Korean] Oh, this…

748
00:42:35,053 --> 00:42:39,515
PRODUCTION AND ENVIRONMENTAL
SCIENCE LABORATORY, LEE GYEONGSU

749
00:42:46,439 --> 00:42:47,440
[maid, in English] <i>Excuse me, sir.</i>

750
00:42:49,067 --> 00:42:51,110
[♪ tense music playing]

751
00:42:51,194 --> 00:42:54,614
Mr. Kurokawa, Ms. Shirahama has arrived
at the residence.

752
00:42:54,697 --> 00:42:56,449
Shall I escort her in to see you?

753
00:42:57,658 --> 00:42:58,659
Bring her in.

754
00:42:58,743 --> 00:43:00,661
[maid] Yes, sir. I'll return in a moment.

755
00:43:19,514 --> 00:43:20,515
[in Korean] This guy is…

756
00:43:22,266 --> 00:43:24,268
[♪ ominous music playing]

757
00:43:26,938 --> 00:43:31,067
[in English] He's just… this man
that used to visit when I was little,

758
00:43:31,150 --> 00:43:33,402
and he was always really kind to us.

759
00:43:35,446 --> 00:43:37,448
[♪ music continues]

760
00:43:55,133 --> 00:43:56,384
Hello, Karin.

761
00:44:14,193 --> 00:44:16,487
MERRY BERRY LOVE

762
00:44:16,571 --> 00:44:17,572
NEXT EPISODE

763
00:44:17,655 --> 00:44:18,739
[Yubin] <i>Mr. Kurokawa is shady.</i>

764
00:44:18,823 --> 00:44:21,284
- Green Nova is…
- [Kurokawa] <i>I thought by now</i>

765
00:44:21,367 --> 00:44:23,369
<i>they would have given up trying.</i>

766
00:44:23,452 --> 00:44:26,164
I have to get them back, no matter what.
They have to be protected.

767
00:44:26,247 --> 00:44:27,415
[Kurokawa]<i>Take any measures necessary.</i>

768
00:44:27,498 --> 00:44:28,499
[Yubin panting]
